Proteomics QC
The QC panel summarizes and exports:

sample total intensity;
sample missing-value rate;
intensity boxplots;
intensity density;
PCA based on variable features;
coefficient-of-variation distribution;
the normalized matrix.

Outputs
The module reports the number of proteins, taxa and functions and provides:

merged abundance/taxonomy/function table;
taxonomy composition plot;
function composition plot;
taxon-function Sankey diagram;
taxon-function heatmap;
downloadable merged table.

Outputs
The module provides:

a GSEA result table;
a top-pathway dotplot;
a single-pathway enrichment curve using GseaVis;
CSV export of all GSEA results;
PDF export of the dotplot and enrichment curve.







WarningGSEA is not the same as over-representation analysis



GO/KEGG enrichment in the preceding chapter starts from a selected ID set. GSEA instead tests coordinated movement across a ranked list, which can detect pathway-level signals even when individual proteins do not cross a hard significance threshold.
